QuestGuidance.Register("en",214,{
[6817]="7007213C\n1\tTalk to Numûru\tYou have arrived in the Emax Dûl guard barracks. You should talk to Numûru.\n2\tFind the armoury\tThe barracks appear to have been abandoned. You should look around and find the armoury.\n3\tCollect Ordâkhai weapons (total: 5)\tYou have found the armoury. You should collect Ordâkhai weapons.\n4\tFend off the Ordâkhai ambushers\tYou are being ambushed by Ordâkhai! You should deafeat the Ordâkhai attackers.\n5\tTalk to Numûru\tYou have survived the ambush. You should talk to Numûru.\n6\tDefeat the Utûgi\tAn Utûgi captain and his followers block your exit. You should defeat the Utûgi.\n",
[6818]="7005A657\n1\tTalk to Hetbrúda\tTalk to Hetbrúda.\n2\tFind a good location to spy on the Orcs\tFind a good location to spy on the Orcs.\n3\tListen to the Orc factions\tListen to the Orc factions.\n4\tDefeat the remaining hobgoblins\tDefeat the remaining hobgoblins.\n5\tTalk to Gazathrug\tTalk to Gazathrug.\n6\tDefeat Gazathrug\tDefeat Gazathrug.\n",
[6819]="7006EEE7\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Dun Shûma\tSpeak with Mizâdi on the battlefield outside Dun Shûma.\n2\tDefeat Ekhamâti at Dun Shûma (total: 16)\030Destroy tar pots on the battlefield (total: 5)\tDefeat Ekhamati forces and destroy Ekhamâti tar pots as you move toward the hilltop.\n3\tTake the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces\tTake the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces.\n4\tDefend the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces until reinforcements arrive\tDefend the hilltop from Ekhamâti forces until reinforcements arrive! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tSpeak with Mizâdi on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Khûd Zagin on the hilltop outside of Dun Shûma.\n6\tSet up camp on the hilltop outside of Khud Zagin.\t\n7\tSet up barricades around the hilltop encampment (total: 3)\tSet up barricades around the hilltop encampment.\n",
[6820]="7006EEE8\n1\tMake your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi\tMake your way down the hilltop and toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi.\n2\tMake your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi\tMake your way toward the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma with Mizâdi.\n3\tDefeat Ekhamâti forces at Dun Shûma (total: 12)\030Treat the wounded Subuzûri (total: 6)\tDefeat Ekhamâti forces and treat the wounded Subuzûri at Dun Shûma. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tEnter the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma\tEnter the inner courtyard of Dun Shûma.\n5\tDefeat the Ekhamâti forces\tDefeat the Ekhamâti forces! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tListen to Mizâdi and Bârshud II\tListen to Mizâdi and Bârshud II.\n7\tDefeat the Mûmak\tDefeat the Mûmak!\n8\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Dun Shûma.\n",
[6821]="7006C4B3\n1\tEnter the passage from Ub Nishir\tEnter into the passage from Ub Nishir to begin the attack on the Orcs in Maurûsh.\n2\tFollow Galâmka through the passage\tFollow Galâmka through the passage to reach Maurûsh. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat the Orcs\tOrcs have ambushed you inside the passage to Maurûsh. Defeat them! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tFollow Galâmka through the passage\tYou have defeated the Orc ambush. Follow Galâmka as he leads you through the passage to Maurûsh. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tDefeat the Orcs\tMore Orcs have spotted you and want to prevent you from reaching Maurûsh. Defeat them and continue the fight. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tContinue through the passage\tContinue following Galâmka through the passage to get to the stronghold of Maurûsh. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n7\tSpeak with Galâmka\tYou have arrived at the entrance into Maurûsh. Speak with Galâmka when you are ready to continue the fight.\n8\tExit the passage into the stronghold of Maurûsh\tProceed out of the passage and into the stronghold of Maurûsh to continue the battle. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n9\tDefeat the Orcs guarding the stairs\tThe fight in Maurûsh continues. You must push your way up the stairs to bring the battle to the leader of the Orcs. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n10\tReconvene with Galamka at the top of the stairs\tReconvene with Galamka at the top of the stairs in the stronghold of Maurûsh to bring the fight to the leader of the Orcs here. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n11\tDefeat Râkdakul and reclaim Maurûsh\tYou have made it to Râkdakul, the Utûgi who is leading the Orcs here in Maurûsh. He must be stopped so the stronghold can be reclaimed. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n12\tEscape Maurûsh back to the mountain passage\tRâkdakul and the Orcs proved too powerful. Escape Maurûsh back into the mountain passage! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n13\tEscape Maurûsh back to the mountain passage\tRâkdakul and the Orcs proved too powerful. Escape Maurûsh back into the mountain passage!\n",
[6822]="7000F103\n1\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is standing on the slope that winds past the small dwarf-outpost in view of the still pool. You have come with Bósi along the winding path that runs up to the Hollin Gate, and he is waiting to speak with you.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tThe small outpost along the path that winds up to the still pool in front of the Hollin Gate is under attack. Bósi and the dwarves need your help to defend the outpost from the shadow-wolves.\n3\tBring repaired pick-axes to Wárr\tWárr is supervising work at the Hollin Gate, east of the small outpost and around the pool. While Bósi helps make preparations at the small outpost, he wants you to deliver the repaired pick-axes to Wárr at the Hollin Gate.\n4\tPlace repaired pick-axes in the crate\tThe crate is located south of Wárr and next to Brogur, in front of the Hollin Gate. Wárr has asked you to leave the repaired pick-axes in a crate for future use.\n5\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in front of the Hollin Gate. Brogur is waiting to speak with you about helping the expedition at the Hollin Gate.\n6\tInteract with Sebbi\030Interact with Rókur\030Interact with Bori\tDwarves throwing stones into the water can be found along the shores of the pool. Brogur has a bad feeling about the pool in front of the Hollin Gate and has asked you to get the dwarves to stop disturbing the water.\n7\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is outside the Hollin Gate. You have gotten the dwarves to stop disturbing the waters of the pool outside the Hollin Gate, and should return now to Brogur.\n8\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is outside the Hollin Gate. Bósi has arrived and is waiting to speak with you.\n9\tUse Rubble\tSome large stones have blocked the Doors of Durin, which stand in the Walls of Moria at shore of the Black Pool. Bósi believes it would be an honour for you to help in clearing some of the rubble from the Hollin Gate.\n10\tWait for more dwarves to arrive\tThe dwarves are gathered on the edge of the pool outside the Hollin Gate. The Hollin Gate is nearly opened, and the dwarves prepare to enter the mines.\n11\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is on the edge of the pool outside the Hollin Gate, with the rest of the dwarves of his expedition. The Hollin Gate is nearly opened, and the dwarves prepare to enter the mines, but something has made you uneasy.\n12\tRemain on your guard\tSomething, or many somethings, are lurking in the waters of the pool!\n13\tReturn to the small outpost and get help\tThe small outpost is on the other side of the pool, where you defended Bósi from attacking shadow-wolves. The dwarves are attempting to fight off the mysterious creature that lurks now outside the Walls of Moria. Bósi has ordered you to hurry to the small outpost to seek help for the desperate dwarves.\n14\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is at the small outpost where you fought the shadow-wolves, on the other side of the menacing pool. The dwarves are in full retreat from the mysterious creature in the pool, and you should speak to Bósi before the expedition turns into a rout.\n",
[6823]="70020F03\n1\tTalk to Dagoras\tSpeak with Dagoras and find a way to release him from his cell.\n2\tFind the key to Dagoras' cell\tFind the key to Dagoras' cell in the jailor's quarters.\n3\tFind the key to Dagoras' cell in the jailor's quarters.\t\n4\tRelease Dagoras from his cell\tRelease Dagoras from his cell.\n5\tTalk to Dagoras\tEscape from Lhe Lhechu with Dagoras.\n6\tHelp Dagoras escape\tEscape from Lhe Lhechu with Dagoras.\n7\tTalk to Dagoras\tSpeak with Dagoras again.\n",
[6824]="700649F6\n1\tTalk to Finrúth\tFinrúth is prepared to tell the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Finrúth.\n2\tListen to Finrúth's tale\tFinrúth is recounting the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.\n3\tTalk to Finrúth\tFinrúth is ready to continue the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Finrúth.\n4\tListen to Finrúth's tale\tFinrúth is recounting the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.\n5\tTalk to Finrúth\tFinrúth is ready to continue the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Finrúth.\n6\tListen to Finrúth's tale\tFinrúth is recounting the tale of her time among the Iron Crown at Mount Gundabad.\n",
[6825]="70000D81\n1\tFind Bounder Primstone\tBounder Primstone is somewhere within the goblin-caves and may be in trouble! Halros has sent you to find Bounder Primstone beneath the Greenfields before something happens to him.\n2\tTalk to Bounder Primstone\tBounder Primstone was wounded in the caves deep beneath the Greenfields. You have found Bounder Primstone, but he has been hurt by the goblins.\n3\tTalk to Halros\tHalros has found his way into Lubach's \"throne room\" at last and is waiting to speak with you about your victory.\n",
[6826]="7006B592\n1\tTalk to Corudan in your dream\tThe hallway outside the tower room in the Citadel of Winds swims from the recesses of your sleeping mind.\n2\tEnter the tower room in your dream\tThe unnatural flames barring the way into the tower room high within the Citadel of Winds have disappeared, granting you passage.\n3\tExamine the image of Balakhôr the Scourge conjured by your dreaming mind\tThough he has been dead for months, the image of Balakhôr the Scourge glowers at you from the other side of the tower room.\n4\tListen to familiar voices conjured by your dreaming mind\tFamiliar images and voices emerge from your dreaming mind.\n5\tTalk to Corudan in your dream\tThe tower room in the Citadel of Winds swims from the recesses of your sleeping mind.\n6\tMaintain focus as your dream continues\tYou are gripped with a sense of unreality as an unfamiliar land coalesces before your sleeping eyes.\n7\tExamine the image of the Grim Southron conjured by your dreaming mind\tYou expected your dreaming mind to bring you a vision of the grove of Arwáth, but it is not so. It seems the course of your dream is not so easily-controlled.\n8\tListen to unfamiliar voices conjured by your dreaming mind\tUnfamiliar images and voices emerge from your dreaming mind, of events you never could have seen.\n9\tExamine the scorpion conjured by your dreaming mind\tYour dreaming mind conjures unusual images before you, with familiar voices emerging from unexpected places.\n10\tMaintain focus as your dream continues\tAn image from the darkest corner of the Morgul Vale swims from the recesses of your mind.\n11\tExamine the image of Mithrandir conjured by your dreaming mind\tIn your dream the Wizard Mithrandir stands before an unpleasant statue in the Valley of the Secret Shadow.\n12\tWitness the strange images conjured by your dreaming mind\tThe dream feels so real to you.\n13\tTalk to Mithrandir in your dream\tThuringwath swims hazily before your dreaming eyes.\n",
[6827]="700443DD\n1\tTalk to Bingo by the bridge into Rohan\tBingo is ready to cross into the kingdom of Rohan.\n2\tTalk to Willem on the other side of the bridge\tWillem is on the southern side of the bridge, in the kingdom of Rohan.\n3\tTalk to Egwylf\tA woman of Rohan has galloped up the road, impressed at your victory over the Orc raiding party.\n4\tListen to what Egwylf has to say of Rohan\tYou have met a woman named Egwylf just within the border of Rohan, and she is very interested in the adventures of your small party.\n5\tTalk to Bingo\tBingo is on the southern side of the bridge, in the kingdom of Rohan.\n",
[6828]="7000041F\n1\tSpeak to Constable Underhill\tConstable Underhill travelled with you to the cave hideout of William Skunkwood, the former leader of the Blackwolds in the area of Combe. Skunkwood is dead, as well as a good many other brigands, but you must be certain they have not begun to muster their strength again.\n2\tSpeak to the brigand\tIn one of the deeper chambers of the Blackwolds' hideout, you encountered the mysterious dwarf threatening a brigand. The dwarf gravely wounded the brigand, then fled, commanding his dwarves to attack you. Constable Underhill has asked you to speak to the wounded brigand.\n3\tSpeak to Constable Underhill\tThe dying brigand revealed that the Blackwolds were being paid by both someone from the south and agents of Angmar. When he tried to reform the band without allegiance to either, the Pale Dwarf struck him down. You should speak with Constable Underhill about this.\n",
